Level 6: Argument Parsing

Mission: Write a script that accepts a filename as an argument and prints the number of lines in that file. If no filename is provided, display a message saying 'No file provided'.

This level we work with functions and arguments that are passed into them.
It is relatively easy where if a file is entered it is parsed through and the number of lines are printed.
If no filename is passed in we provide the message "no file provided".
We can also solidify this script by making sure that directories are also accounted for if they are passed in as a variable. 

To check if a file is inputed we can use the $# function which checks how many arguments were inputted. 

We input the file and then run it through a while loop using the read command to run through each line.
